## 2. Performance Optimization

### ✅ DO

- Use `React.memo` for expensive components that receive stable props
- Use `useCallback` for functions passed as props or used in dependencies
- Use `useMemo` for expensive calculations
- Use Zustand selectors to prevent unnecessary re-renders
- Enable `useNativeDriver: true` for all animations
- Use `FlatList` or `FlashList` for long lists (never map arrays > 20 items)
- Optimize images: set width/height, use appropriate formats, add `loading="lazy"`
- Debounce search inputs and frequent API calls

### ❌ DON'T

- Subscribe to entire store when only needing one property
- Create inline functions in render (causes re-renders)
- Use `useEffect` without proper dependencies
- Render large lists without virtualization
- Load large images without optimization

**Example - Bad:**

```typescript
// ❌ Subscribes to entire store, re-renders on any change
const store = useUserStore();

// ❌ Creates new function on every render
<Button onPress={() => doSomething()} />

// ❌ Missing dependency
useEffect(() => {
  fetchData(userId);
}, []); // userId not in deps
```

**Example - Good:**

```typescript
// ✅ Selective subscription
const user = useUserStore((state) => state.user);

// ✅ Memoized callback
const handlePress = useCallback(() => {
  doSomething();
}, []);

// ✅ Proper dependencies
useEffect(() => {
  fetchData(userId);
}, [userId]);
```

