## 5. TypeScript & Type Safety

### ✅ DO

- Enable strict mode in tsconfig.json
- Define proper types for all props, functions, and API responses
- Use type inference where clear
- Create shared types in `src/types/`
- Use generic types for reusable components
- Type all Zustand stores

### ❌ DON'T

- Use `any` type (use `unknown` if truly unknown)
- Use `as` type assertions without good reason
- Ignore TypeScript errors with `@ts-ignore`
- Leave function parameters untyped

**Example - Bad:**

```typescript
// ❌ No types
function handleSubmit(data) {
  api.post('/submit', data);
}

// ❌ Using any
const [user, setUser] = useState<any>(null);
```

**Example - Good:**

```typescript
// ✅ Properly typed
interface FormData {
  phoneNumber: string;
  otp: string;
}

function handleSubmit(data: FormData): Promise<void> {
  return api.post('/submit', data);
}

// ✅ Proper type
const [user, setUser] = useState<User | null>(null);
```

