## 6. React Native Specific Rules

### ✅ DO

- Use `SafeAreaView` from `react-native-safe-area-context` for proper notch handling
- Use Platform-specific code when needed (`Platform.OS === 'ios'`)
- Handle keyboard properly with `KeyboardAvoidingView` or `react-native-keyboard-controller`
- Use `useNativeDriver: true` for all Animated API calls
- Add proper accessibility props (`accessibilityLabel`, `accessibilityRole`)
- Test on both iOS and Android

### ❌ DON'T

- Use web-only APIs without polyfills
- Forget to handle keyboard on forms
- Use inline styles for everything (use NativeWind classes)
- Ignore safe areas on modern devices

**Example - Bad:**

```typescript
// ❌ No native driver
Animated.timing(fadeAnim, {
  toValue: 1,
  duration: 300,
}).start();

// ❌ No accessibility
<TouchableOpacity onPress={handlePress}>
  <Text>Submit</Text>
</TouchableOpacity>
```

**Example - Good:**

```typescript
// ✅ Native driver enabled
Animated.timing(fadeAnim, {
  toValue: 1,
  duration: 300,
  useNativeDriver: true,
}).start();

// ✅ Proper accessibility
<TouchableOpacity
  onPress={handlePress}
  accessibilityLabel="Submit form"
  accessibilityRole="button">
  <Text>Submit</Text>
</TouchableOpacity>
```

