## 7. API & Networking

### ✅ DO

- Use the service layer (`src/services/`) for all API calls
- Implement proper error handling with try-catch
- Use interceptors for auth headers and token refresh
- Handle network errors gracefully
- Show loading states during API calls
- Implement retry logic for failed requests
- Use raw axios (not apiClient) for token refresh to avoid circular deps

### ❌ DON'T

- Make API calls directly in components
- Ignore error responses
- Create circular dependencies in API/auth modules
- Block UI without loading indicators
- Make sequential API calls that could be parallel

**Example - Bad:**

```typescript
// ❌ API call in component
function UserProfile() {
  useEffect(() => {
    axios.get('/user').then(setUser);
  }, []);
}

// ❌ No error handling
async function getUser() {
  const response = await apiClient.get('/user');
  return response.data;
}
```

**Example - Good:**

```typescript
// ✅ Service layer
// src/services/user/user-api.ts
export async function getUser() {
  return apiClient.get<User>('/user');
}

// ✅ Proper error handling
async function fetchUserData() {
  try {
    setLoading(true);
    const response = await getUser();
    setUser(response.data);
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Failed to fetch user:', error);
    showError('Could not load user data');
  } finally {
    setLoading(false);
  }
}
```

