## 8. Authentication Patterns

### ✅ DO

- Separate auth logic into service layer
- Store tokens in MMKV/SecureStore only
- Implement token refresh in API interceptor
- Check auth status on app start (in SplashScreenController)
- Clear all auth data on logout (tokens + user store)
- Redirect to login on 401/403 errors
- Use protected routes with guards

### ❌ DON'T

- Store tokens in Zustand store
- Import auth-service from api-client (circular dependency)
- Skip auth validation on app start
- Leave stale tokens after logout

**Example - Circular Dependency to Avoid:**

```typescript
// ❌ BAD: Creates circular dependency
// auth-api.ts -> api-client.ts -> auth-service.ts -> auth-api.ts

// ✅ GOOD: Use auth-utils for shared logic
// auth-utils.ts (no dependencies on auth-api or api-client)
export function clearAuth() {
  tokenStorage.clearTokens();
  useUserStore.getState().actions.clearData();
}
```

