## 10. Code Quality & Maintainability

### ✅ DO

- Write self-documenting code with clear names
- Add JSDoc comments for complex functions
- Remove unused imports and code
- Keep functions small and focused (< 50 lines)
- Use early returns to reduce nesting
- Extract magic numbers to constants
- Follow consistent naming conventions:
  - camelCase for variables/functions
  - PascalCase for components/types
  - UPPER_CASE for constants

### ❌ DON'T

- Leave commented-out code
- Use abbreviations in names (except common ones: `id`, `url`, `api`)
- Write functions that do multiple things
- Nest conditionals more than 3 levels deep

**Example - Bad:**

```typescript
// ❌ Unclear name, does too much
function handleData(d) {
  if (d) {
    if (d.id) {
      if (d.id > 0) {
        // deep nesting
        const res = api.post('/data', d);
        if (res.ok) {
          return res.data;
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

**Example - Good:**

```typescript
// ✅ Clear names, single responsibility, early returns
async function saveUserProfile(profile: UserProfile): Promise<void> {
  if (!profile?.id || profile.id <= 0) {
    throw new Error('Invalid profile ID');
  }

  const response = await api.post('/user/profile', profile);

  if (!response.ok) {
    throw new Error('Failed to save profile');
  }
}
```

