## 11. NativeWind/Tailwind Styling

### ✅ DO

- Use Tailwind classes via className prop
- Use design tokens from global.css (colors, spacing)
- Create reusable styled components for common patterns
- Use responsive classes when needed
- Follow the existing design system

### ❌ DON'T

- Mix inline styles and Tailwind unnecessarily
- Create custom colors outside design tokens
- Hardcode sizes (use Tailwind scale)

**Example - Bad:**

```typescript
// ❌ Inline styles
<View style={{ padding: 16, backgroundColor: '#007aff' }}>

// ❌ Non-standard spacing
<View className="p-[17px]">
```

**Example - Good:**

```typescript
// ✅ Tailwind classes with design tokens
<View className="p-4 bg-primary">

// ✅ Using design system
<View className="px-4 py-2 bg-card rounded-lg">
```

